 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs with an irregular yo form",
     "texto": [
      "In the present tense, several very common verbs change only in the **yo** form:\n\n| Verb | yo | tú |\n|---|---|---|\n| hacer | **hago** | haces |\n| salir | **salgo** | sales |\n| poner | **pongo** | pones |\n| traer | **traigo** | traes |\n| dar | **doy** | das |\n| ver | **veo** | ves |\n| decir | **digo** | dices |\n| oír | **oigo** | oyes |\n\n**Hacer** means both do and make: hago los deberes, hago la cena. **Poner la mesa** is to lay the table. **Salir de** is to leave a place; **salir con** is to go out with someone.\n\n**Tener** and **venir** also have a g in the yo form: **tengo**, **vengo**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Yo forms in use",
     "texto": [
      "In these sentences the verbs have the irregular **yo** form: **salgo**, **oigo**, **hago**. The pronoun **yo** can often be dropped, but here it is kept to show who does the action. With a negative, Spanish keeps both words: **no hago nada**."
     ],
